    "contrast": "Required minimum WCAG 2.1 ratio. null explicitly means no contrast requirement (not missing data).",
    "background": "Virtual semantic token for the actual terminal background; its hex is anchored by the recipe, not a Pi theme slot.",
    "terminalForeground": "Virtual token for unstyled terminal text. Derived in reference themes; pin measured RGB with --terminal-fg for a real terminal.",
    "backgrounds": "Each entry expands into its own pair. Text colors on different surfaces may need different ratios.",
    "kind": "text checks glyphs; nonText checks graphical marks or colored surfaces.",
    "proposed": "Token proposed for Pi but not supported yet. The extended target emits it; the current target omits it and applies its rules to `fallback`, the color Pi renders there today. A terminalForeground fallback models Pi's \"\" (terminal default).",
    "targets": "Optional. Limits a rule to the current and/or extended target, for rules that differ once proposed tokens and Pi remappings exist."
